WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:00.863
- Okay.

00:00:00.863 --> 00:00:04.150
So, I've been wanting to make
this video for a long time,

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.610
and I'm still not totally confident

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:09.420
that I have the exact
words that I want to say,

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.690
but I am pretty passionate
about this concept.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:15.030
And I think there is sort of
a toxic narrative in the world

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:18.770
today, sort of an overprescribed
antidote to a crappy life.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.050
And that is to follow your dreams.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:24.130
Other iterations of this
can be land your dream job,

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.690
find your dream husband or dream wife,

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:28.340
live in your dream house.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:32.250
This whole idea of following
your dreams sounds really good

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.410
and emotional, and it can get you excited.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.930
And you might say, well, I'm
in a really crappy place.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:40.820
And the idea of eventually
landing my dream job

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:41.680
gives me hope.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.210
What's wrong with developing
a vision for my life

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.753
and chasing that vision with all my heart?

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.060
Well, there's a couple
of things wrong with it

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.520
because I think if you
follow that train of thought,

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.680
you might actually find
that you'll be less happy,

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:56.870
not more happy because you'll be focusing

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.080
on the wrong things.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.330
I'm not saying it's completely useless.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.580
There is something to be said

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.730
about say, landing your dream job.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.440
What you do for a living does
take up a considerable portion

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:08.290
of your day.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.830
And if you absolutely hate what you do,

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.730
then it's probably pretty
difficult to enjoy yourself

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:17.140
or for the experience of life
to be something pleasant,

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.500
something that you enjoy interacting with.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.250
But at the same time
you've heard, I've heard,

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:25.310
and everyone on this
earth has heard stories

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.870
of people who are technically
living their dream job.

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:30.010
People who have made it,

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:33.670
people who are extremely
successful and are miserable,

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:37.420
and empty inside and they
maybe even kill themselves.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.350
So, what's with that?

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.040
Where's the disconnect?

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.980
They probably followed their dreams,

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:45.490
but also neglected so many
aspects of their lives

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:48.500
that actually contribute
to their overall happiness.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.090
And I can relate to this pretty heavily.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.610
Ever since I was 12 years old,

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.420
I thought it would be so
cool to be a YouTuber.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.980
And I made like 10 to 15
channels throughout my teen hood,

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:01.050
sketch comedy with my
friends, action movies.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.030
I've even tried movie reviews.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.650
So often I would fantasize
about the one day

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:07.180
where a video blew up,

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.180
and my channel will be just like lifted

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:10.090
off the ground.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:13.030
And I wouldn't have to
scoop dog poop for a living,

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.050
or deliver mattresses
up 10 story buildings.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.370
And I was like, "Oh,
I could be a YouTuber.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.210
That would be so cool. I could
wake up whenever I wanted to.

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:22.000
I can make movies with my friends.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.410
I could pour my heart
and soul into what I do

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.780
and actually enjoy it."

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.350
And it happened and I'm a YouTuber now,

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.320
and I have over a million
subscribers and that's incredible.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.400
And it is incredible.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.960
But one thing that I didn't
factor into my calculations

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:39.270
as a kid is that I would
be the exact same person

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:42.850
that I was before and
after landing my dream job,

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:43.770
or making it.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.970
I'm the exact same person.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:49.750
And the experience of what
it feels like to be me,

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:53.130
doesn't change regardless
of what I do for a living,

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:56.550
and any sort of tendency to
postpone my own happiness,

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:59.710
to wait for some day where
I'll figure it all out.

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:01.970
I can't be happy now.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:03.050
Things aren't good enough yet.

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:06.350
I can't be happy about who I
am. I'm not good enough yet.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.950
Those tendencies remained and yes,

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.997
I landed my dream job, but I
constantly find myself like,

00:03:11.997 --> 00:03:13.580
"No, I haven't made it yet."

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.230
I haven't reached the next level yet.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:16.610
I can't start dating people.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:18.780
This isn't the best version of me yet.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.850
The world hasn't seen who
I can actually become,

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:23.030
but it's poisonous.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.770
This postponing your happiness is toxic.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:26.603
And I feel like this,

00:03:26.603 --> 00:03:29.720
"follow your dreams"
sentiment really fuels that.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.090
It makes us forget that so much happiness

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.880
can be found in our present moment.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.690
And I think it's so foolish
to sacrifice relationships

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:40.430
with your friends, your
family, your mental health,

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:42.570
your spiritual life, your physical health,

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.670
in the pursuit of following your dreams.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:48.580
Finding that one thing
that truly makes you happy,

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.770
and makes everything make sense.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:54.640
You're delegating responsibility
to some hypothetical.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.410
You're letting go of
the reins of your life,

00:03:56.410 --> 00:04:00.000
and the responsibility of
forging your own happiness

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.900
in life as it is.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:02.990
And rather, you're just saying,

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:04.190
you're relinquishing control.

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:06.350
You're saying, "Ah, this version sucks.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:07.610
I want the next version."

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:09.310
And I just think that's an endless game.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.730
Unless you break that cycle early,

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.620
you can be hamster wheeling yourself like

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.550
that right into your grave.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:19.280
So, rather than following your dreams,

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.890
why not make today your dreams
as cheesy as that sounds.

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:26.090
Why not make your average day something

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:27.650
that you really enjoy doing?

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.590
Why not repair the relationships

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:30.940
that are already in your life?

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:33.970
Why not spend more time with
the people that you care about?

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:37.710
Why not work on your
habits, work on your body,

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.950
develop a better
relationship with yourself.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:42.100
Work on your mental health,
your physical health,

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.920
your spiritual health, and yes,

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.690
have hopes and dreams for the future.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.140
Otherwise you're directionless,

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.410
but don't forget to keep one foot grounded

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:53.010
in the present moment and
stop to smell the roses

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:56.333
because life is a journey,
not a destination.

00:04:56.333 --> 00:04:57.210
(laughs) All of these things.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:59.440
It's so funny with like
"follow your dreams,"

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.600
and "life is a journey,
not a destination."

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:02.940
There's so many cliches.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.270
It's like hard to figure out which ones

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:06.960
actually are good advice,

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:09.480
but I feel like there's
truths to all of them,

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:12.290
but none of them are absolute truths.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:15.450
Your own happiness and fulfillment
in life is such a blend

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.230
of a multitude of factors.

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:19.650
But anyways, yeah, like
imagine for a second

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.730
that you are a horribly miserable person.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:24.010
Maybe you don't have to imagine,

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:28.460
but imagine you are resentful
and you are anxious,

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:31.580
and you're restless and you're depressed.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:36.580
And there's like the seed
of insecurity, of anxiety,

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:41.840
and of just pain at the
core of your existence.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:45.900
Maybe that's you right now,
and I've absolutely been there.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.200
And you feel this feeling,

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.630
this is the experience of being you.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:54.660
This is what being you feels
like when there's no music

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.450
to drown you out. No TV
shows to distract you.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:00.690
Now, if you bring this ball,

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:04.080
if you bring this soul
into a new job position,

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.390
that's technically on paper
or what you want to do

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:10.590
for a living, this experience
will still be there.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:13.740
This feeling of being
you will still be there.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:16.580
And the conditions of your
existence won't necessarily

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:19.090
change the nature of your existence.

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:21.560
If you want to change the
nature of your existence,

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:22.970
then you need to accept it.

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:24.347
You have to stop running from it.

00:06:24.347 --> 00:06:27.290
And you have to listen to
it and give it air time,

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:30.430
and like figure out what
your insecurities are.

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:31.720
Work through them.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.100
Maybe that's through
therapy, good friendships,

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.420
heart to hearts.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:37.670
And maybe that is taking
care of your body.

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:40.410
And maybe that is having
more fulfilling hobbies.

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:45.090
Like it's so much to have
that feeling of being you,

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:49.340
something that is enjoyable and
free and happy and peaceful.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.560
So, that's the important thing.

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:55.590
If you are miserable, work
on your misery directly,

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:58.580
accept it, figure out what
the actual feeling is,

00:06:58.580 --> 00:06:59.760
and how you can resolve it.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.940
I can almost guarantee
you that it's a lot deeper

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.180
than just what you do for a living,

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:07.830
or whatever condition that you're sort of

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:09.930
externalizing your problems onto.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.430
Let's figure out what the
core of the issue is here,

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:14.760
and that way landing your dream job,

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.230
or following your dreams,

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:19.720
or making your dreams come
true will become a lot less

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:20.660
of a necessity.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:23.110
You can find peace and fulfillment sooner

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:24.510
than you might think.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.343
So, yeah.

